  "headline": "The masker is NOT what varies across strata -- detection is. Mask AP50 ranges 0.217 (<10 crowns/tile) to 0.684 (>=80), but box AP50 tracks it almost exactly, and the mask-minus-box gap stays in a narrow +0.012..+0.042 band and is POSITIVE in every stratum. On the closure axis the gap even rises slightly with canopy closure (+0.0247 open -> +0.0326 closed), i.e. the commonality assumption does not visibly degrade where a reviewer would predict it should. Weakest strata are sparse tiles and the Lower Gangetic Plains biome (0.260), and both are detection-limited."
